I'd use `.lower()` for uppercase letters and `.upper()` for lowercase ones. So I could probably loop through the string and build a new one. Like this:

res = ""
for char in string:
    if char.isupper():
        res += char.lower()
    elif char.islower():
        res += char.upper()
    else:
        res += char
return res

It would just be:

def flip_case(string: str) -> str:
    return string.swapcase()
